
## Engine half (RA) + acceptance test

- The earlier queue agent's work sat uncommitted (fmt red, no commit); fixed and
  committed with the engine wiring below.
- RA: `EvaEmissionQueue<RaEvaLine>` wired into `Game` (field), ticked every
  `update()`, `speak()` called at the real emission sites: construction complete,
  structure destroyed, unit lost, base under attack (35s), low power (transition),
  canceled, superweapon launch, mission accomplished/failed (TriggerHost win/lose).
- `ra_eva_emits_on_gameplay_events` (plan acceptance) drives a scripted skirmish
  through those real sites and harvests >=8 distinct lines; also pins one-slot
  semantics (second speak in a tick is dropped).
- Notes discovered while testing: `recompute_power` overwrites `house.power` each
  tick, so a deficit needs the real lever (powering plants off). Win/lose lines
  only emit from the trigger actions (TriggerHost::win/lose), not from setting
  `outcome` directly. Superweapon lines come from TACTION 1_SPECIAL firing.

